-- erwartet: N056
-- **A `falsifier` that resolves to something which cannot refute -- and the checker
-- waved it through.** Measured against the unchanged checker on 2026-09-04:
-- `assume a "…" falsifier zaehler;` beside `extern fn zaehler() -> u64` checked with
-- `3 items, 0 errors, 0 hints`, exit=0. A `u64` is a value, not a verdict: nothing in
-- that function can ever say "refuted", so the assumption carries a probe that cannot
-- go red -- an assurance about the ABSENCE of a refutation (R14, R15, W10).
--
-- **The pass does NOT demand that the name resolve at all.** A probe is a C program in
-- `sonden/`, not a declaration (`namen.rs`, decided 2026-08-19; `sonden/README.md`
-- carries the same point under a heading of its own). 89 of the corpus's 98 `falsifier`
-- clauses resolve to nothing and stay green. This one resolves -- and that is what makes
-- it checkable.
--
-- The `-> never` twin (a watchdog that guards no loop) is the second arm of the same
-- rule; this probe carries the value arm alone so that only one message can fire.
module gift::falsifier_ohne_ausgang {

extern fn zaehler() -> u64 effects { pure } costs <= 1 ops;

assume a "The timer ticks." falsifier zaehler;

}
